Expected elements: present

Every Must-show item is on the page. The provenance marker is present in form (c) — a `Data` row at the top of the Overview grid carrying the `Real Aztec mainnet data` badge and the capture's own sentences — and it is the only one of the three forms present, so the absent band is correctly not a finding. `Not observable` badge, the published pruning reason, the permanence claim, full hash, outcome badge, block/canonical/finality/cost, all four content sections with permanent-tense statements, nav, footer, disclosure and provenance strip are all there. Nothing forbidden appears: no debug/retry/spinner, no trace reference, no danger tone.

Density is the page's weakness. The `Data` row is ~260px tall against ~40px for each of Block, Canonical, Finality and Cost, so 62% of the facts grid is one narrative cell and the four scannable facts are compressed into the last fifth of the card. The page then uses 911px of a 1920px viewport at its widest and 697px for every notice card — two right edges 213px apart — so a 9-line paragraph is stacked above facts that a second column would have carried beside it.

The `Decoded input` note is worse than dense: it is wrong. Over `SELECTOR —` and `RAW 0x`, with `bodyRetainedAtCapture: false` in the raw block, it claims parameters are shown as raw bytes and offers a fix that cannot work.

Fixes: correct the Decoded input note; move the capture narrative out of the first grid row.

Rating: 4/10

